[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      224[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// A tie needs the double's exact value to be `m / 10^5` with `m` ending in 5;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      225[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// since doubles are dyadic, `m / 10^5 = m / (2^5 * 5^5)` forces `5^5 | m`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      226[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// every possible tie is an odd multiple of `1/32`. This group sweeps odd
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      227[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// multiples of `1/2^k` for `k = 1..=5` across the whole integral mantissa
