[1mPublic API.[22m [38;5;10mdriver.h[0m exposes a single function, [38;5;10mvoid driver(double)[0m. It prints one line with three glibc conversions of the same value: [38;5;10m%llx[0m of the raw bits, [38;5;10m%a[0m, and [38;5;10m%.4f[0m. There is no call hierarchy below it, so the test groups instead stratify the input space and the failure reporter attributes any mismatch to the specific conversion that diverged.[0m[0m
