[1mTests[22m ([38;5;10mtranslation/tests/[0m), all going through [38;5;10mlibloading[0m — the Rust side is [38;5;10mdlopen[0med from the release [38;5;10mcdylib[0m and called via [38;5;10mdlsym("driver")[0m, never as a direct Rust call:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mharness/mod.rs[0m builds both libraries on demand (cmake for C, [38;5;10mcargo build --release[0m into a separate target dir so it cannot deadlock on the target lock), then compares output by pointing fd 1 at a temp file around each batch of calls.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mdriver_compare.rs[0m — 11 groups, ~565k inputs by default: specials/NaN payloads/subnormals, all 2098 powers of two, [38;5;10m%.4f[0m rounding ties, the full exponent sweep, mantissa nibble patterns, integer neighbourhoods via bit-adjacent values, decimal literals across 41 decades, and three random sweeps. [38;5;10mDRIVER_TEST_RANDOM=5000000[0m was also run clean (12.5M inputs).[0m[0m
