[1mTie-breaking, the one real risk area.[22m [38;5;10m%.4f[0m can only hit an exact rounding tie when the value is an odd multiple of 1/32 (a tie needs [38;5;10mm/10⁵[0m with [38;5;10mm[0m ending in 5, and dyadic representability forces [38;5;10m5⁵ | m[0m). The [38;5;10mdyadic_ties[0m group sweeps that set directly across every binary exponent instead of relying on random sampling to stumble into it. Rust's [38;5;10m{:.4}[0m and glibc's [38;5;10m%.4f[0m agree on all of them, confirming both round half-to-even.[0m[0m
