[1mHarness caveat worth knowing.[22m My first run showed 6 "mismatches" that were entirely artifacts: libtest's own progress output from parallel test threads was landing in the captured fd 1. Since fd 1 is process-global, the comparisons now live in a single [38;5;10m#[test][0m and the harness flushes both Rust's and libc's stdout before swapping the descriptor. I confirmed the harness still catches real bugs by injecting three mutations ([38;5;10m%.5f[0m precision, dropping the [38;5;10m%a[0m exponent sign, shifting the subnormal exponent) — each was caught and correctly attributed to its conversion — then restored the original source.[0m[0m
